# Admiral host driver for the agent-teammates scripts, used when ADMIRAL_SHIP is non-empty (for HARNESS codex or copilot, not
# under ADMIRAL_AUTOPILOT=1). The operations and their contract are in ../CONTRACT.md. Teammates are Admiral crew boats
# (`admiral crew launch|send|list|close`), so Admiral is the viewer and VIEWER in team.env is ignored. A boat's session id is its
# crew name. The exception is a read-only Codex or Copilot teammate, which runs headless under its harness driver: the
# declarations below are the crew boats', and such a teammate works one turn at a time (LIVE_MESSAGING=0).
LIVE_MESSAGING=1
SEND=script
# SKILL_PREFIX is deliberately absent: this driver defers it to the run harness, so commodore's role-skills.sh keeps reading it
# from drivers/$HARNESS.
# Per-run state: <team-dir>/admiral-delegated, one id per line, written only by `launch` for a read-only Codex/Copilot teammate
# handed to its harness driver. Otherwise none: `status`, `stop` and `tail` read `admiral crew list --json`.
# has-skill, list-skills and advisor-probe run the run harness's operation as is.
